WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.849
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:09.455
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:16.877
Unit four: Reported Speech: Statements, Questions and Commands. Today you will report what other people said correctly.

4
00:00:17.177 --> 00:00:19.864
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.870
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:25.567
Report.

7
00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:28.920
Report means to tell what someone said.

8
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:31.005
She reported the news.

9
00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:34.199
Your turn. Say: Report.

10
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:37.965
Report.

11
00:00:38.717 --> 00:00:39.741
Backshift.

12
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.842
Backshift means moving a tense back.

13
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.183
Backshift changes will to would.

14
00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:48.145
Your turn. Say: Backshift.

15
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.955
Backshift.

16
00:00:52.717 --> 00:00:53.985
Reporting verb.

17
00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:57.772
Reporting verb means a verb like say or tell.

18
00:00:58.383 --> 00:01:00.058
Say is a reporting verb.

19
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.767
Your turn. Say: Reporting verb.

20
00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.983
Reporting verb.

21
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:09.613
Ask.

22
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:12.756
Ask means to request information.

23
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.723
He asked me a question.

24
00:01:15.317 --> 00:01:17.690
Your turn. Say: Ask.

25
00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:21.360
Ask.

26
00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:22.851
Tell.

27
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.244
Tell means to give information to someone.

28
00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.002
She told me to wait.

29
00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:31.118
Your turn. Say: Tell.

30
00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:34.724
Tell.

31
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:36.252
Order.

32
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.062
Order means to say that someone must do something.

33
00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.127
He ordered us to stop.

34
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:44.963
Your turn. Say: Order.

35
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:48.569
Order.

36
00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:50.120
Whether.

37
00:01:51.117 --> 00:01:54.173
Whether means used in reported yes/no questions.

38
00:01:54.783 --> 00:01:56.388
He asked whether I was ready.

39
00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.415
Your turn. Say: Whether.

40
00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:03.047
Whether.

41
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:04.796
Yesterday.

42
00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:07.911
Yesterday means the day before today.

43
00:02:08.517 --> 00:02:10.238
He said it happened yesterday.

44
00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:13.317
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

45
00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.261
Yesterday.

46
00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:21.381
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.217 --> 00:02:25.946
Visal, how do I change direct speech into reported speech?

48
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:37.957
Move the tense one step back and change pronouns and time words. I am tired becomes She said that she was tired, and tomorrow becomes the next day.

49
00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.515
What about questions?

50
00:02:41.617 --> 00:02:53.467
Use normal word order, not a question order, and no question mark. Where do you live becomes He asked where I lived. Yes/no questions use if or whether.

51
00:02:54.583 --> 00:02:55.770
And commands?

52
00:02:56.883 --> 00:03:06.736
Use tell or ask plus an infinitive. Close the door becomes She told me to close the door. Do not open it becomes He told us not to open it.

53
00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.424
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:13.374
Grammar focus: Reported speech patterns.

55
00:03:13.674 --> 00:03:14.849
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.201
She said that she was tired.

57
00:03:18.117 --> 00:03:19.756
He asked me where I lived.

58
00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:29.610
Move the tense back, change pronouns and time words, and keep statement word order in reported questions. Use tell plus an infinitive for commands.

59
00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.885
Be careful! Don't say: He asked me where did I live.

60
00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:38.332
Say: He asked me where I lived.

61
00:03:38.632 --> 00:03:39.831
Statement order.

62
00:03:40.633 --> 00:03:43.042
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:45.252
What the Teacher Said.

64
00:03:45.552 --> 00:03:48.167
The teacher said that the exam would be on Friday.

65
00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.712
She asked us whether we had finished the project.

66
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.351
She told us to bring a pen.

67
00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:56.948
She told us not to be late.

68
00:03:57.933 --> 00:04:00.177
Then she asked where the library was.

69
00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:05.129
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:05.983 --> 00:04:08.981
I am tired → She said she blank tired.

71
00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:12.656
A, be. B, was. C, is.

72
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.793
The answer is B: was.

73
00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.518
A reported question uses blank word order.

74
00:04:21.818 --> 00:04:25.100
A, question. B, no. C, statement.

75
00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.655
The answer is C: statement.

76
00:04:31.817 --> 00:04:34.582
Close the door → She told me blank the door.

77
00:04:34.882 --> 00:04:38.466
A, to close. B, closing. C, close.

78
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.162
The answer is A: to close.

79
00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.921
Tomorrow becomes blank.

80
00:04:47.221 --> 00:04:51.235
A, today. B, the next day. C, yesterday.

81
00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.811
The answer is B: the next day.

82
00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.182
A yes/no question uses blank.

83
00:05:00.482 --> 00:05:03.787
A, that. B, what. C, if or whether.

84
00:05:07.333 --> 00:05:09.124
The answer is C: if or whether.

85
00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:13.694
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:17.249
Report: She said, 'I will help you.'

87
00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.585
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:27.885 --> 00:05:35.556
She said that she would help me. I change will to would and I change the pronouns. I keep the sentence as a statement.

89
00:05:35.856 --> 00:05:37.635
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:43.037
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reported speech patterns.

91
00:05:43.337 --> 00:05:47.243
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

92
00:05:47.543 --> 00:05:50.358
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

93
00:05:50.658 --> 00:05:53.101
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

